BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Poetry Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260929T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260929T150000
UID:6a7b7d58be1482002986a238@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Come join us for a creative afternoon of poetry and discussion
 . Bring in your original poems or poems that you admire. Share your word
 s in a supportive atmosphere\, respond to the poems of others\, receive wr
 iting tips\, and explore the works of a wide range of contemporary poets.\
 nThis is a drop-in program\, no registration required.
LOCATION:Taylor Memorial\, Meeting Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a7b7d58be1482002986a238
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Adult Afternoon Movie - Orwell: 2+2=5 (2025)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261006T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261006T160000
UID:6a527647f8c7897403624b28@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:The ultimate and comprehensive documentary film about the exce
 ptional writer George Orwell. A film directed by Raoul Peck that utilizes
  archival footage\, excerpts from a wide range of other films\, and the au
 thor's own personal letters and journals.\nPG\, 119 minutes\, documentary\
 n**Subtitles for the Deaf and Hard of Hearing (SDH) when available.
LOCATION:Riverdale\, Program Room 1
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a527647f8c7897403624b28
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Power of the Pen: Handwriting Analysis
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260914T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260914T140000
UID:6a85e6a160ccaf01c01f64e9@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Come prepared to laugh and learn during Elaine's "Power of the
  Pen" while you discover how to communicate even more effectively with fam
 ily and friends through knowing what the strokes of handwriting mean.  Ev
 eryone will learn about their strengths as reflected in the 'paper mirror'
  of their handwriting.  Elaine will be e-mailing Handwriting Profiles to 
 the Participants who fill out the Handwriting Form!
LOCATION:Barbara Frum\, Located in Room B on the third floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a85e6a160ccaf01c01f64e9
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Seniors E-Connect
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260919T103000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260919T120000
UID:6a8ddad4aafa6100295f07c8@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Seniors E-Connect matches older adults with a teen volunteer t
 o provide tech help\, under the guidance of library staff. Learn the basic
 s of using mobile devices\nand learn about topics such as library e-resour
 ces. Get one on one support in a welcoming and friendly environment.\nPlea
 se register with your phone number if you want to be reminded with a phone
  call.  One registration per person.  Do not register twice\, contact s
 taff to confirm if needed.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal i
 nformation on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under t
 he Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The informat
 ion will only be used for event and program registration\, delivery and ev
 aluation. Questions about how the library handles your information can be 
 directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 
 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Bridlewood\, Youth Hub
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a8ddad4aafa6100295f07c8
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Moving Stories: Arts-based movement class for older adults
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260929T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260929T113000
UID:6a26cef0f56bd86e00b548a2@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Tiger princess dance projects\n\, a non-profit contemporary da
 nce company\, brings you a free custom designed arts-based movement class 
 for older adults. Join Artistic Director Yvonne Ng and her team of profess
 ional artists in a fun\, healthy\, and exciting arts program\,\nMoving Sto
 ries\n.\nThese free classes offer an introduction into the enriching world
  of art and creativity through movement and music. These activities have p
 roven to improve circulation\, retain joint mobility\, promote mental stim
 ulation\, improve posture and coordination\, and build strength and balanc
 e.\nNo previous movement experience required.\nSuggested Age: 60 +\nGo at 
 your own pace\, modifications encouraged\nExercises can be modified for se
 ated movement and/or standing
LOCATION:Leaside\, Community Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a26cef0f56bd86e00b548a2
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
