BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Finding Recovery Through Exercise Skills and Hope (FRESH): Movies 
 Saturdays
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260912T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260912T163000
UID:6931f2a276261f28005d7d63@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This program helps people stay active\, make friends\, learn n
 ew skills\, and have fun. Meet new folks\, build connections\, and tell us
  about programs and services you would like to see in the neighbourhood!\n
 Come and join the F.R.E.S.H. group for a Saturday screening of popular mov
 ies.\nWe'll be playing the following films\nSeptember 5th –\nPapillon (
 1973)\nSeptember 12th –\nCabaret\nSeptember 19th –\nWhat's Eating Gilb
 ert Grape\nSeptember 26th –\nMoonlight\nDrop in\, no registration is req
 uired.\nSnacks and refreshments are provided for all participants. Ingredi
 ent lists will be available at the program.\nThis program is in collaborat
 ion with\nGerstein Crisis Centre's F.R.E.S.H. initiative\n.
LOCATION:Toronto Reference Library\, First floor\, Activity Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6931f2a276261f28005d7d63
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Adult Crafternoon
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261124T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261124T153000
UID:6a7b75fa4c610f0038947888@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Craft and socialize in a friendly and welcoming environment at
  our monthly adult and seniors crafternoon!  All materials provided.\nCons
 ider wearing clothes that you don't mind getting messy.\nSeptember - Step-
 By-Step Acrylic Painting - Aspen Tree\nOctober - Cork Pumpkin\nNovember - 
 Holiday Ornament\nDecember - Step-By-Step Acrylic Painting - Holiday Edit
 ion\nDrop in. Space is limited to 25 participants.  Arrive early to secure
  a spot!
LOCATION:Richview\, Room A\, 2nd Floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a7b75fa4c610f0038947888
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:An Edible History of Toronto
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260917T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260917T200000
UID:6a7e344ca821f90037eda982@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Toronto is a global culinary capital\, home to iconic food bra
 nds and restaurants\, from Café Diplomatico to Mr. Christie's Cookies. Bu
 t how did Toronto earn its reputation as a foodie haven? Join culinary his
 torian Dr. Laura Carlson on a mouth-watering journey through Toronto’s f
 ood history. Bring your appetite and your stretchy pants for a virtual tas
 te of past and present Toronto.\nDrop in\, no registration required.
LOCATION:Brentwood\, Community Room\, Ground Floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a7e344ca821f90037eda982
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
