BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Romance Book Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261008T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261008T200000
UID:6a9a0ecf36204e08fbb97cf1@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Welcome to the Romance Book Club\, where love stories take cen
 ter stage and every page promises a new adventure of the heart. Whether yo
 u're into slow burns\, second chances\, or enemies-to-lovers\, there's som
 ething here for every kind of romantic. Come read\, swoon\, and share your
  favorite moments with fellow book lovers.\nThe winning title for Brentwo
 od's Romance Book Club on Thursday October 8 is\nThe Charm Offensive\nby
  Alison Cochrun.\nWe will save 5 minutes at the end of the meeting to disc
 uss the second place title\,\nGet a Life\, Chloe Brown\nby Talia Hibbert
 .\nLimited copies will be available in branch for pick up from September 3
 .\nPlease note that this book club is for individuals 18+.\nDrop in\, no r
 egistration required.\nThe Charm Offensive\nGet A Life\, Chloe Brown\nNote
 : At this meeting we will be voting on Brentwood's November Romance Book C
 lub title.
LOCATION:Brentwood\, Community Room\, Ground Floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a9a0ecf36204e08fbb97cf1
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Finding Recovery Through Exercise Skills and Hope (FRESH): Music A
 ppreciation
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261008T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261008T153000
UID:6a79e77a88e9bf280036db4c@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This program helps people stay active\, make friends\, learn n
 ew skills\, and have fun. Meet new folks\, build connections\, and tell us
  about programs and services you would like to see in the neighbourhood!\n
 Join us and share your favourite song of the moment\, or a song that means
  something to you. Discover new music\, and meet other folks that share yo
 ur love of music.\nDrop-in\, all are welcome.\nSnacks and refreshments are
  provided for all participants. Ingredient lists will be available at the 
 program.\nThis program is in collaboration with\nGerstein Crisis Centre's 
 F.R.E.S.H. initiative\n.
LOCATION:Fort York\, Program Room
