BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Letters to Amelia: Author Talk
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261026T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261026T150000
UID:6a7385b73f18b57d52339ed0@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Celebrate Women's History Month with Toronto-based author and
  letter writer Lindsay Zier-Vogel who discusses\n“Letters to Amelia”\
 n\, her debut novel inspired by her passion for Amelia Earhart\, and the p
 ower of reading and writing letters for both connection and self-discovery
 .\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form i
 s collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\,
  sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for
  event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about
  how the library handles your information can be directed to Answerline st
 aff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON
  M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Mount Pleasant\, Basement program room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a7385b73f18b57d52339ed0
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:How Pleasant to Know Mr. Lear
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261126T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261126T150000
UID:6a751cd8f213992f00ca3065@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Dennis Duffy\, Professor Emeritus\, Department of English\, U
 niversity of Toronto\, discusses the genius of Edward Lear as a painter a
 nd poet\, the great joiner of oil painting and printed nonsense.\nLear was
  a singular eccentric in his bespoke but loosely-fitting suits and his run
 cible hat\, he created work placing him among the finest of graphic cartoo
 nists and satirists. This presentation explores that jagged world that he 
 made up for himself\, in order to preserve his own complex selfhood.\nInfo
 rmation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is colle
 cted by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sectio
 ns 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event 
 and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how th
 e library handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\
 nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G
 8.
LOCATION:Mount Pleasant\, Basement program room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a751cd8f213992f00ca3065
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Mimico Book Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261017T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261017T120000
UID:6a873d93db86e4004d867ef0@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Our book selection for October is\nTitus Groan\nby Mervyn Peak
 e\, an eccentric and epic novel about the inhabitants of a vast\, isolat
 ed castle ruled by the Groan family. By turns fantastical\, comical\, and 
 dramatic\, Groan and its sequel\, Gormenghast\, is regarded as one of the 
 greatest and most unique achievements in fantasy literature.\nCopies avail
 able at the library.\nThe Gormenghast Trilogy
LOCATION:Mimico Centennial\, Meeting Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a873d93db86e4004d867ef0
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
