BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Book Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261117T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261117T150000
UID:6a31965e7550c8bf9f5dcde8@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:***PLEASE NOTE THE DATE CHANGE FROM WED. NOV. 18 to TUES NOV. 
 17***\nJoin us for a lively and fun discussion about the selected book.\nS
 ept:\nVioleta\nby Isabel Allende\nOct:\nA Town Called Solace\nby Mary Laws
 on\nNov:\nA Gentleman in Moscow\nby Amor Towles\nDec:\nCreation Lake\nby R
 achel Cushner\nPlease place a copy of the book on hold\, limited quantitie
 s may be made available
LOCATION:Richview\, Room B\, upstairs
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a31965e7550c8bf9f5dcde8
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Senior Movie Day
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260929T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260929T160000
UID:6957e964e3e3999b5c0551dc@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a relaxing afternoon movie\, designed specificall
 y for seniors\, held every last Tuesday of the month! Whether you're a fil
 m lover or just looking for a way to unwind with good company\, our Senior
  Movie offers a welcoming environment to enjoy classic films\, new release
 s\, or nostalgic favorites.\nApril 28 - The Farewell (2019)\nMay 26 - Moth
 er's Day (2016)\nJune 23 - Indian Horse (2017)
LOCATION:Eglinton Square\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6957e964e3e3999b5c0551dc
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Finding Recovery Through Exercise Skills and Hope (FRESH): Movies 
 Saturdays
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260919T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260919T163000
UID:6931f2a276261f28005d7d64@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This program helps people stay active\, make friends\, learn n
 ew skills\, and have fun. Meet new folks\, build connections\, and tell us
  about programs and services you would like to see in the neighbourhood!\n
 Come and join the F.R.E.S.H. group for a Saturday screening of popular mov
 ies.\nWe'll be playing the following films\nSeptember 5th –\nPapillon (
 1973)\nSeptember 12th –\nCabaret\nSeptember 19th –\nWhat's Eating Gilb
 ert Grape\nSeptember 26th –\nMoonlight\nDrop in\, no registration is req
 uired.\nSnacks and refreshments are provided for all participants. Ingredi
 ent lists will be available at the program.\nThis program is in collaborat
 ion with\nGerstein Crisis Centre's F.R.E.S.H. initiative\n.
LOCATION:Toronto Reference Library\, First floor\, Activity Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6931f2a276261f28005d7d64
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Canadian Council of the Blind Book Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261021T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261021T120000
UID:6a8eedf060ccaf01c0212145@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This book club is facilitated by staff in partnership with the
  Canadian Council of the Blind\, Toronto Visionaries Chapter. The book clu
 b is open to those who are living with vision loss or have low vision or a
 re deaf-blind\, and to their sighted support workers. The book club meets 
 on the third Wednesday of every month. October's book is\nWhat Strange Par
 adise\nby Omar el Akkad.
LOCATION:Deer Park\, Main Floor Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a8eedf060ccaf01c0212145
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
