BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:La Scopa: Learn and Play a Traditional Italian Card Game
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260921T133000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260921T150000
UID:6a85ec1fbe14820029887e54@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Scopa (Italian: [ˈskoːpa]\; lit. 'broom') is a century old t
 raditional Italian card game\, involving memory\, skill\, strategy and lit
 tle bit of luck. It is easy to learn\, and a challenge to master. Bring yo
 ur friends or make new ones while playing this classic pass time.
LOCATION:Humber Summit\, Auditorium\, Lower level
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a85ec1fbe14820029887e54
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Newcomer Settlement Services
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261020T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261020T170000
UID:69c1d0efbfe6da1042250b04@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:New to Canada? Need information on employment\, housing\, lang
 uage learning\, schools\, or other topics? A Settlement Worker can help. D
 rop in to meet our settlement worker every Tuesday afternoon from 2 pm-5 p
 m.\nVisit our branch or contact Ada Tao at 416-770-0312 or atao@cathcrossc
 ultural.org.\nIn partnership with Catholic Crosscultural Services.\nPlease
