BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Royal Conservatory of Music & Telus Centre
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260923T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260923T200000
UID:6a832b259d8416003f69c765@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This beautiful 1880s Toronto Baptist College building\, now th
 e Royal Conservatory of Music\, was sensitively restored in the early 21st
  century. The catalyst was the addition of the innovative Telus Centre for
  Performance and Learning. Through dozens of photographs\, architectural h
 istorian Marta O'Brien will discuss the exteriors and interiors of this wo
 nderful complex dedicated to music education and performance.\nDoors open 
 at 6:30pm\nPresented in collaboration with North Toronto Historical Societ
 y.
LOCATION:Northern District\, Room 200
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a832b259d8416003f69c765
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Newcomer Settlement Services
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261103T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261103T170000
UID:69c1d0efbfe6da1042250b06@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:New to Canada? Need information on employment\, housing\, lang
 uage learning\, schools\, or other topics? A Settlement Worker can help. D
 rop in to meet our settlement worker every Tuesday afternoon from 2 pm-5 p
 m.\nVisit our branch or contact Ada Tao at 416-770-0312 or atao@cathcrossc
 ultural.org.\nIn partnership with Catholic Crosscultural Services.\nPlease
  bring your immigration documents (PR card) with you
LOCATION:Albert Campbell\, Front Entrance
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69c1d0efbfe6da1042250b06
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:NatureTO: Our Urban Forest
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261104T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261104T153000
UID:69a1e4a2491b809c6f1cf550@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Toronto has one of the largest urban forests in the world. Joi
 n the City of Toronto Urban Forestry staff for an in-library presentation 
 on this amazing natural habitat that reaches all corners of Toronto.\nWe
 ’ll discuss what makes the urban forest so special and share tools to he
 lp you explore and understand it better. Bring questions and curiosities\,
  and leave with greater confidence and a deeper understanding of your City
  and the natural world around you!
LOCATION:Taylor Memorial\, meeting room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69a1e4a2491b809c6f1cf550
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
