BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Ask a Sommelier: Navigating Wine Labels\, Lists\, and Restaurant E
 tiquette
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261006T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261006T200000
UID:6a85e17a2d60e40d5b5b6269@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Learn to make smarter decisions as a consumer when buying wine
  in a store or in a restaurant. Sommelier Christopher Lafleur will make ap
 proaching a wine list (and the ritual around the first taste) make so much
  more sense by breaking down what is on labels\, teaching what terms are u
 seful\, and what terms don't mean anything.\nDrop-in\, but space is limite
 d.\n*\nSpecial guest for the\nTuesday Cards and Chitchat program.
LOCATION:Guildwood
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a85e17a2d60e40d5b5b6269
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Bone Health 101
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260925T133000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260925T150000
UID:6a7e113fb20478002992af85@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:At least 1 in 3 women and 1 in 5 men will suffer from a fragil
 ity fracture in their lifetime. Join a volunteer facilitator from Osteopor
 osis Canada and learn how to improve your bone health\, reduce your risk o
 f osteoporosis and related fractures by exploring the following:\nWhat you
  need to know about bone health and osteoporosis\nThe risk of fracturing a
  bone\nHow to maintain healthy bones\nImpact of nutrition & physical activ
 ity Fall prevention
LOCATION:St. Clair/Silverthorn\, Community Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a7e113fb20478002992af85
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
