BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Blatant Injustice The Internment of Jewish Refugees in Canada duri
 ng World War II
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261103T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261103T193000
UID:6a8f51104cb69d003e2398cf@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Author Ian Darragh talks about his book chronicling the harrow
 ing experiences of Jewish refugees to Canada\, who were treated as enemies
  and imprisoned in internment camps during World War II. Yet the internees
 \, who were Holocaust survivors\, did not let the authorities crush their 
 spirit. Blatant Injustice is a story of resilience and determination.
LOCATION:Yorkville
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a8f51104cb69d003e2398cf
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Creative Connection:  Collaborative Painting for Seniors
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261014T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261014T153000
UID:6a85e1532cbfe80d71a47aa4@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This interactive painting workshop for seniors encourages crea
 tivity\, social connection\, and confidence through a fun and guided exper
 ience. Participants will create a collaborative artwork by painting in pai
 rs\, combining imagination with simple step-by-step instruction. No experi
 ence is needed. The focus is on enjoyment\, creativity\, and meaningful so
 cial interaction in a relaxed environment.\nRegistration Required. Space i
 s limited.\nRegister online or call 416-396-8872.\nRegistration opens Sept
 ember 14\, 2026\n.\n*\nSpecial guest for the\nWednesday Seniors Social pro
 gram.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this fo
 rm is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries A
 ct\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used
  for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions a
 bout how the library handles your information can be directed to Answerlin
 e staff at answerline@tpl.ca\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto O
 N M4W 2G8
LOCATION:Guildwood
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a85e1532cbfe80d71a47aa4
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
