DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261027T160000
UID:6a612391f4e5db3d00c38dd1@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:The renowned psychiatrist Lilian Steiner (Jodie Foster) mounts
  a private investigation into the death of one of her patients (Virginie E
 fira)\, whom she is convinced has been murdered.\nR\, 105 minutes\, spoken
  French\n**Subtitles for the Deaf and Hard of Hearing (SDH) when available
 .
LOCATION:Riverdale\, Program Room 1
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a612391f4e5db3d00c38dd1
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Elmbrook Book Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261126T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261126T200000
UID:69fbc6fef89ee1580051092b@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us the last Thursday of each month to discuss that month'
 s title.  Haven't read the book?  Join us anyway to hear what others have 
 to say and meet new people. This is a drop in program.\nJuly 30 -\nMigrant
  Rain Falls in Reverse\nby\nVinh Nguyen\nAugust 27 -\nWhere’d You Go\, B
 ernadette?\nby Maria Semple\nSeptember 24 -\nMinistry of Time\nby\nKaliane
  Bradley\nOctober 29 -\nGreat Believers\nby\nRebecca Makkai\nNovember 26 -
 \nBlack Wolf\nby\nLouise Penny
LOCATION:Elmbrook Park\, Program room
