BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Computers for Beginners 6: Use Gmail
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261005T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261005T153000
UID:6a6129ea4523092f0031e28c@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Learn to use Gmail\, Google's free web-based email service.\nI
 n this sixth session you will:\nPractice basic email functions: send\, rea
 d\, reply\, forward\, delete email\, and attach files\nReview how spam and
  junk mail work\nUpon completion of this class students will have a basic 
 understanding of how to use email.\nInstructions on how to set up and mana
 ge your own free Gmail account are included in the handout.\nPrerequisites
 : Basic keyboarding and mouse skills required.\nFormat: Hands-on with demo
 nstrations.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on t
 his form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libra
 ries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only b
 e used for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Quest
 ions about how the library handles your information can be directed to Ans
 werline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, 
 Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Riverdale\, Program Room 1
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a6129ea4523092f0031e28c
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Adult Afternoon Movie - The Choral (2025)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261103T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261103T160000
UID:6a6125f2e9de6536001d92a8@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:1916. As war rages on the Western Front\, the choral society o
 f Ramsden\, Yorkshire has lost most of its men to the army. The Choral's a
 mbitious committee\, determined to press ahead\, decides to recruit local 
 young males to swell their ranks. They must also engage a new chorus maste
 r\, and despite their suspicions that he has something to hide\, their bes
 t bet seems to be Dr. Henry Guthrie (Ralph Fiennes) driven\, uncompromisin
 g\, and recently returned from a career in Germany. As conscription papers
  start to arrive\, the whole community discovers that the best response to
  the chaos that is laying waste to their lives is to make music together.\
 nR\, 113 minutes\n**Subtitles for the Deaf and Hard of Hearing (SDH) when 
 available.
LOCATION:Riverdale\, Program Room 1
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a6125f2e9de6536001d92a8
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Financial Workshops for Seniors
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261015T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261015T160000
UID:6a8c4fe960ccaf01c02085db@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Presented by John Stapleton from Open Policy Ontario\, learn m
 ore about government programs\, benefits and eligibility criteria for seni
 ors. These sessions are designed for seniors with low income and those who
  advise them.\nThursday Oct 1: What Do Seniors Get?\nLearn about benefits
  for older adults living in Ontario\, including Canada Pension Plan (CPP)\
 , Old Age Security (OAS)\, Guaranteed Income Supplement (GIS)\, and Guaran
 teed Annual Income Supplement (GAINS).\nThursday Oct 15: Understanding the
  Personal Income Tax System.\nWhat is a taxable income and how can tax cre
 dits\, deductions\, entitlements and exemptions help to reduce taxable inc
 ome.\nThursday Oct 29: Protecting Your Retirement Income.\nLearn how to re
 duce claw backs to GIS and GAINS payments if receiving additional income 
 from employment\, a private pension\, or a Registered Retirement Savings P
 lan (RRSP).\nThursday Nov 12: Coming to Canada and Leaving Canada.\nLearn 
 about eligible benefits for those that resided in Canada for fewer than 4
 0 years between the ages of 18 and 65\, or for those planning on emigratin
 g from Canada after retiring.\nThursday Nov 26: Tax Credits and Benefits f
 or Seniors and People with Disabilities.\nLearn about other tax credits an
 d benefits for seniors\, people with disabilities\, and caregivers\, inclu
 ding the disability tax credit\, the Canada caregiver credit\, and the hom
 e accessibility tax credit.\nRegistration not required. Drop-in welcome.
LOCATION:Queen/Saulter
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a8c4fe960ccaf01c02085db
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
