BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Human Connection 101 Workshop for Seniors
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260917T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260917T153000
UID:6a8b322957c264087ad326b0@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Human connection has a profound impact on our health and happi
 ness\, especially in our increasingly disconnected world. Join GenWell in 
 an interactive workshop to learn practical ways to enhance social health\,
  understand the adverse effects of loneliness\, and discover the benefits 
 of building more meaningful connections. Receive a free social health work
 book\, spend time with other participants after the workshop\, and enjoy s
 ome light refreshments provided.\nAbout GenWell: Founded in 2016\, GenWell
  is a registered charity whose mission is to make the world a happier and 
 healthier place by educating\, empowering\, and catalyzing forty million C
 anadians about the importance of their social health.\nInformation Collect
 ion Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the Tor
 onto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c
 )\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program reg
 istration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handl
 es your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl
 .ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Eglinton Square\, Meeting Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a8b322957c264087ad326b0
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
