BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:How Canadians are Feeling about Democracy These Days
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261014T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261014T193000
UID:6a99ae1baafa610029615271@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Trust in democratic institutions is being tested in Canada and
  around the world. Canadians continue to express support for democratic va
 lues\, yet many are reporting growing concerns about political polarizatio
 n\, declining trust in governments and institutions\, misinformation\, and
  whether political systems are responsive to citizens' needs.\nDrawing on 
 the latest public opinion research\, electoral studies\, and engagement da
 ta\, this panel will examine how Canadians are feeling about democracy tod
 ay. Are concerns about democratic health widespread or concentrated among 
 particular groups? What is driving shifts in political trust and participa
 tion? And what can governments\, civil society organizations\, educators\,
  and communities do to strengthen democratic resilience and engagement for
  the future?\nCheck out the\nKnowYourVote.TO\nwebsite and the\nCelebrate D
 emocracy\npage to learn more about Toronto’s upcoming municipal election
 \, access important voter resources\, and discover activities and interact
 ive library programs for all ages happening at a branch near you.\nThis ev
 ent is generously supported by the McConnell Foundation.\nInformation Coll
 ection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the 
 Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 2
 0(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program 
 registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library ha
 ndles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@
 tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, Concourse Event Space
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a99ae1baafa610029615271
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
