BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Travelling as an Older Solo Woman
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261005T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261005T143000
UID:6a692de67b79214226ac0315@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Solo women travellers are changing the face of travel\, and wo
 men represent the largest single cohort of travellers. For those women who
  acknowledge some barriers to embracing this phenomenon and cite “fear
 ” as the reason\, this presentation will help them understand how they c
 an travel safely\, wisely\, and fearlessly.​\nThis presentation that wil
 l leave you encouraged\, equipped\, and inspired to get out there and expl
 ore your corner of the world and beyond.\nLauraLee Giliberti  has led stud
 ents on tours\, travels alone or with a group\, and prides herself on doin
 g so economically and safely. She also believes one is never too old to li
 ve their best life.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal informat
 ion on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Publ
 ic Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information wil
 l only be used for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluatio
 n. Questions about how the library handles your information can be directe
 d to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge S
 treet\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Woodside Square\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a692de67b79214226ac0315
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Connecting the Dots(?) Book Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261112T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261112T160000
UID:6a11b72b8e677a28001e0617@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Have you ever wondered why people believe in conspiracies?\nIn
  this book club\, we will be reading books that explore the social conditi
 ons that make people prone to extreme belief.\nThurs. Jun. 11\, 2:00-4:00p
 m\nEscaping the Rabbit Hole by Mick West\nThurs. Jul 9\, 2:00-4:00pm\nBlac
 k Pill by Elle Reeve\nThurs. Aug. 13\, 2:00-4:00pm\nProject Mind Control b
 y John Lisle\n**BOOK CHANGE**\nThurs. Sept. 10\, 2:00-4:00pm\nConspiracy: 
 Peter Thiel\, Hulk Hogan\, Gawker\, and the Anatomy of Intrigue by Ryan Ho
 liday\n**BOOK CHANGE**\nThurs. Oct. 8\, 2:00-4:00pm\nThe Brainwashing of M
 y Dad by Jen Senko\nThurs. Nov. 12\, 2:00-4:00pm\nShock Doctrine by Naomi 
 Klein
LOCATION:Toronto Reference Library\, Founder's Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a11b72b8e677a28001e0617
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
