BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Google Docs 1: Create and Edit a File
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260910T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260910T193000
UID:6a8790240c0e3a002aeb0700@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Learn how Google Docs can be a useful free tool when you don't
  have access to Microsoft Word. In this introductory class you will learn 
 how to open\, create\, save and delete Google Docs. Features such as highl
 ight\, bold\, italics\, underline\, font colour and font size will be cove
 red as well as how to use spell check\, print\, and download as Word docum
 ent.\nPrerequisites: Basic mouse and keyboard skills are required.\nFormat
 : Hands-on with demonstrations\nNo Registration\nDrop-ins welcome until ca
 pacity is reached.
LOCATION:Forest Hill\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a8790240c0e3a002aeb0700
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Why We Misunderstand the Middle East—And Why It Matters
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261119T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261119T200000
UID:6a877294aafa6100295e0108@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join Dr. Hamid Yazdi and explore how media narratives\, famili
 ar assumptions\, and everyday language shape public understanding of the 
 region. This talk invites audiences to question simplified explanations an
 d think more critically about what they hear. With real-world implications
  - from public debate to economic ripple effects - getting the Middle East
  right is more important than it seems.\nDrop in\, no registration require
 d.
LOCATION:Brentwood\, Community Room\, Ground Floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a877294aafa6100295e0108
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Canva: Graphic Design & Layout
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260923T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260923T193000
UID:6a87615958433600542abbd4@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Canva is a free-to-use online graphic design tool. Use it to c
 reate social media posts\, presentations\, posters\, videos\, logos and mo
 re.\nEasily create eye catching business cards and flyers. Use Canva's dra
 g-and-drop feature and professional layouts to design consistently stunnin
 g graphics. Create polished work using different templates and techniques 
 that make your creations pop.\nDesign presentations\, social media graphic
 s\, and more with thousands of beautiful layouts.\nIt has everything you n
 eed for amazing design:\nMillions of Stock Images\, Photo Filters\, Free I
 cons & Shapes\, and Hundreds of Fonts.
LOCATION:Agincourt\, Learning Centre
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a87615958433600542abbd4
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
