BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Artists in the Library: Plants are Medicine
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260923T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260923T200000
UID:6a886f1b57c264087ad2b360@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Come and learn to felt and bead while working with plant medic
 ines making massage oils\, bath bombs. A knowledge keeper and healer will 
 join us the first day\, followed by an herbalist and traditional beading f
 acilitator from Kehewin First Nation Register\nSupplies are limited.\nSept
 ember 16 | 6:00–8:00 PM\nIntroduction to\nbody oil-making\n.\nSeptember 
 19 | 10:00 AM–12:00 PM\nBath bomb-making workshop\nSeptember 23 | 6:00
 –8:00 PM\nContinue and complete\nbody oil-making\nIntroduction to\nfelt-
 making\nSeptember 26 | 10:00 AM–12:00 PM\nContinue working with\nfelt\nB
 egin the\nbeading workshop\nSeptember 28 | 6:00–8:00 PM\nContinue\nfelti
 ng\nContinue the\nbeading workshop\nOctober 3 | 10:00 AM–12:00 PM\nWork 
 on\nfelting and beading projects\nOctober 7 | 6:00–8:00 PM\nFeast\nClosi
 ng Circle\nCelebration and completion of the program
LOCATION:Riverdale\, Program Room 1
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a886f1b57c264087ad2b360
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
