BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Digital Expo: AI & Democracy (Livestream)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261003T111500
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261003T161500
UID:6a9095df37716d0d1ad6f93e@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join our Digital Expo panel discussions via livestream from an
 ywhere. Discover how AI is shaping safety\, democracy\, civic participatio
 n and trust\, and explore how we can build AI that advances human flour
 ishing.\nRegistrants will receive an email with a Zoom meeting link within
  24 hours before the program starts.\nLooking to attend in person?\nLearn 
 more and register\n.\nPanel discussions:\nHelping Children Navigate AI Saf
 ely\n11:15 am-12 pm\nExplore how AI is shaping children's lives and lear
 n practical ways to support safe\, responsible and informed AI use at home
  and in school.\nFeaturing Matthew Johnson (MediaSmarts)\, André Côté (
 The Dais)\, and Aarani Stoneham (AI Literacy Learners)\, with moderation b
 y Jessica Wong (CBC).\nSafeguarding Democracy in the Age of AI\n1-1:45 pm\
 nJoin this keynote to examine the opportunities and risks AI presents for 
 democracy\, and the steps needed to strengthen trust\, safety and civic pa
 rticipation.\nFeaturing Beatrice Wayne (Samara Centre for Democracy) and V
 alentine Goddard (AI Impact Alliance).\nAI and Civic Engagement\n2-3 pm\nL
 earn how AI is changing the way people access information\, engage with on
 e another and participate in democracy.\nFeaturing Mathew Markman (Ethelo)
 \, Trevor Potts (Evidence for Democracy) and Lexa Michaelides (Hypha)\, wi
 th moderation by Tai Huynh (The Local).\nFlourishing in an AI Society\n3:1
 5-4:15 pm\nDiscover how communities can help guide AI development toward
  human flourishing\, trust and democratic values.\nFeaturing Victória Old
 emburgo de Mello (Work and Play Lab)\, Jess Mitchell (OCAD University)\, S
 tephanie Jonnson (ODLAN) and Mario Vasilescu (Readocracy)\, with moderatio
 n by Pete Bombaci (Genwell).\n***\nInformation Collection Notice\n: The pe
 rsonal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library
  under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The 
 information will only be used for event and program registration\, deliver
 y and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your information
  can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-3975981
 \, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.\n***
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a9095df37716d0d1ad6f93e
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
